# The registry of image sources. Everything downstream enumerates from
# this file: the pipeline's change detection, the daily staleness check,
# and the merge request opened against the deploy repo.
#
# In the upstream setup each entry is a real git submodule pointing at
# its own source repo. In this public fork the two sample projects are
# checked in under projects/ directly, so the repo is clonable and the
# pipeline is runnable without access to any private repo. The entries
# stay here because they are what the tooling reads.
#
# Both URL styles are shown on purpose. A public project can be fetched
# over HTTPS; a private one needs SSH, and the pipeline loads a key that
# works on both forges (see GIT_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY in .gitlab-ci.yml).
# Note the SSH host and port can differ from the web host.
[submodule "projects/dashboard"]
	path = projects/dashboard
	url = ssh://git@ssh.gitlab.example.com:2224/example-group/dashboard.git
[submodule "projects/docs-site"]
	path = projects/docs-site
	url = https://gitlab.example.com/example-group/docs-site.git
